<sheets>
<sheet>
<plain>
<text x="-27.94" y="111.76" size="1.778" layer="97"> If you want BLE, install connector &amp; wire
 USB 5 Volts on pin 2 to a battery charger.
 Wire battery output to pin 3 and install
 diode D1.</text>
<text x="-48.26" y="96.52" size="1.778" layer="97">Wire to a momentary push button 
switch to reset Pico and port expander</text>
<text x="-88.9" y="86.36" size="1.778" layer="97">Wire to a switch so the Pico W can be
powered off if running from a battery.</text>
<text x="10.922" y="0" size="1.778" layer="97">Install 2 rows of header pins for an FPC
connector breakout board.</text>
<text x="60.96" y="119.38" size="1.778" layer="97">0.1 uF</text>
<text x="-40.64" y="66.04" size="1.778" layer="97">Raspberry Pi Pico for USB or 
Pico W for BLE </text>
<text x="-137.16" y="56.896" size="1.778" layer="97">Add connector and resistors if
controlling a 3.3 volt PS/2 touchpad </text>
<text x="-137.668" y="36.83" size="1.778" layer="97">Add connector to access I2C bus</text>
<text x="21.336" y="131.572" size="1.778" layer="97">Port expander controlled by Pico
via I2C bus at address 0x20 from Pico</text>
<text x="85.852" y="8.89" size="1.778" layer="97" rot="R90">16 Pull Up Resistors</text>
<text x="-109.728" y="4.318" size="1.778" layer="97">X</text>
<text x="-109.728" y="8.89" size="1.778" layer="97">Cut if 5V Jumper installed</text>
<text x="-119.888" y="16.51" size="1.778" layer="97">5V Jumper</text>
<text x="-75.946" y="-22.098" size="1.778" layer="97">GP4</text>
<text x="-132.334" y="-12.192" size="1.778" layer="97">Add connector, resistor, 
&amp; FET if controlling a backlight</text>
</plain>
